ttps://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50514170/cfp-2026-third-committee-top-25-bracket","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest surges into CFP top 12; top 4 unchanged while Texas jumps Notre Dame","description":"Alabama stayed at No. 3 despite some struggles on Saturday while two-loss Texas jumped one-loss Notre Dame for No. 5 in the CFP's latest rankings.","published":"2026-11-18T04:55:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50515993/wake-forest-surges-cfp-top-12-texas-jumps-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pawn shop fighting 'Gold Digger' trademark filed by Jordon Hudson's company","description":"A California pawn shop is opposing a trademark application for \"Gold Digger\" filed by a company connected to Jordan Hudson, then-companion of Bill Belichick.","published":"2026-11-18T00:07:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/50514442/pawn-shop-fights-gold-digger-trademark-filed-hudson","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Anthony Olivieri","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma coach Venables shouts out Love's after Buc-ee's comment","description":"Venables showed love Sunday to Buc-ee's -- which is owned by an alumnus of the Sooners' next opponent, Texas A&M. So on Tuesday the coach repped the Oklahoma-based Love's.","published":"2026-11-17T22:23:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50513199/oklahoma-brent-venables-loves-travel-stop","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-17T21:26:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"North Texas QB Tayven Jackson out with upper-body injury","description":"North Texas senior quarterback Tayven Jackson, who is sixth in the FBS with 3,005 passing yards, will miss at least the next two games with an upper-body injury.","published":"2026-11-17T20:53:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50513204/north-texas-qb-tayven-jackson-upper-body-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Defiant Dabo Swinney says Clemson's 'gonna win a bunch more'","description":"Despite going through a self-described \"rough patch\" over the past two seasons, Clemson coach Dabo Swinney is resolute in his belief that he and the Tigers have a lot more wins ahead of them.","published":"2026-11-17T20:37:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512833/defiant-dabo-swinney-says-clemson-gonna-win-bunch-more","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5117455/ty-benefield","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ty_Benefield"},"pick":{"pick":63,"round":2,"team":"TEN","via":"BUF","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Ty Benefield","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ty_Benefield","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:29Z","intro":"Ty Benefield (born September 4, 2005) is a Canadian college football safety for the LSU Tigers. He previously played for the Boise State Broncos.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Benefield attended Crean Lutheran High School in Irvine, California. During his senior season, he racked up 90 receptions for 1,404 yards and 20 touchdowns. Coming out of high school, Benefield was rated as a three-star recruit by 247Sports and committed to play college football for the Boise State Broncos over offers from other schools such as Washington, Washington State, Oregon State, BYU, Colorado State, and Stetson."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"BOISE STATE\nAs a freshman in 2023, Benefield recorded 46 tackles. In 2024, he started all 14 games, notching 82 tackles, two interceptions, and two fumble recoveries. In 2025, Benefield started all 14 games, recording 105 tackles, three pass deflections, two interceptions, a forced fumble, and a fumble recovery, earning first-team all-Mountain West honors. After the season, he entered his name into the NCAA transfer portal."}]}}